<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qajar capture of Shiraz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1791</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Qajar conquest of Shiraz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> was the taking of the Zand capital by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar">Agha Mohammad Khan Qajar</a> in 1791. According to the site it completed the formal dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a>. Agha Mohammad Khan was later crowned Shah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, founding the Qajar dynasty.</p></div>
